From: chelovechishee <261262090+chelovechishee@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 32/38] power: supply: s2m-charger: set currents from the MUIC
 BC1.2 result without a MUIC node

On the Galaxy Tab A 10.1 2019 the USB-C port is behind an S2MM005 CC
controller and there is no MUIC node; the bootloader leaves the input limit
at 500 mA. Without a muic child, read VBUS and MUIC DEV1 on the vbus/attach/
detach interrupts and set the vendor kernel's input/charge currents
(DCP 1500/2300 mA, CDP 1500/1500, otherwise 500/500), the float voltage from
monitored-battery, and report input/charge current and voltage. gta3xlwifi:
pmic@3d on i2c_1 with its IRQ (gpa2-2).

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/exynos7904-gta3xlwifi.dts |  14 +-
 drivers/mfd/sec-common.c                      |   8 +-
 drivers/power/supply/Kconfig                  |   2 +-
 drivers/power/supply/s2m-charger.c            | 155 +++++++++++++++++-
 4 files changed, 169 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7904-gta3xlwifi.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7904-gta3xlwifi.dts
index 40be269eb..c94c9f9bb 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7904-gta3xlwifi.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7904-gta3xlwifi.dts
@@ -368,9 +368,21 @@ fuel-gauge@3b {
 	};
 };
 
-/* S2MU005 charger/MUIC/flash at 0x3d */
 &i2c_1 {
 	status = "okay";
+
+	/*
+	 * S2MU005 charger/MUIC/flash. No muic node: the USB-C port is behind
+	 * the S2MM005 CC controller; the charger driver reads the MUIC's BC1.2
+	 * result itself.
+	 */
+	pmic@3d {
+		compatible = "samsung,s2mu005-pmic";
+		reg = <0x3d>;
+		interrupt-parent = <&gpa2>;
+		interrupts = <2 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+		monitored-battery = <&battery>;
+	};
 };
 
 &usi2 {
